(a) The administration of this article, including the duty of prescribing forms, is vested in the city manager, except as otherwise specifically provided. The police chief, city zoning administrator, and city code enforcement officer shall render assistance in the administration and enforcement of this article as follows:
(1) The police chief shall make police department facilities and personnel available to photograph an applicant for a license. The cost of photographing shall be paid by the applicant at the time the service is provided. Photographs so obtained shall be maintained by the city clerk in the normal course of business.
(2) The police chief shall have a criminal history inquiry conducted on all persons listed as applicants in a license application. The inquiry shall be limited to determining whether an applicant for a license has a criminal conviction for a specified criminal act or for an act described in section 10-708(c)(13), for the period indicated. The police chief shall notify the city manager if such criminal conviction is found to exist.
(3) The city zoning administrator shall notify the city manager whether an applicant or designated license holder in a license application has failed to comply with or is in violation of applicable provisions of the zoning ordinances, or other land use ordinances and regulations of the city relating to the business to be operated under the license.
(4) The city code enforcement officer is responsible for inspecting establishments in order to ascertain compliance with all applicable building codes, statutes, ordinances and regulations, and shall notify the city manager whether an applicant or designated license holder in a license application has failed to comply with or is in violation of applicable provisions of this article governing the design, construction, and maintenance of the premises where the sexually oriented business is or is proposed to be operated.
(5) The Newton County Fire Marshal is responsible for inspecting establishments and businesses in order to ascertain compliance with all applicable fire codes, statutes, ordinances, and regulations.
(6) Nothing in this section 10-702(a) is intended to prohibit or restrict the police chief or zoning administrator from providing additional assistance as may derive from their normal duties and responsibilities, or as may be requested by the city manager. In no event shall any assistance as described in this section, or the absence of such assistance, delay or extend the time period specified in section 10-711 for the city manager to act on a license application.
(b) An application for a license or for the renewal of a license made pursuant to this article shall be submitted to the city manager, who shall grant or deny the application in accordance with the provisions of this article. The city manager also shall suspend or revoke a license in accordance with the provisions of this article.
(c) A license issued pursuant to this article shall expire on December 31st of the year in and for which it is issued and may be renewed annually.
(d) A license, if granted, shall state on its face:
(1) The name and address of the license holder;
(2) The name and address of the licensed premises;
(3) The date of issuance of the license;
(4) The particular classification of sexually oriented business for which the license is granted; and
(5) The license number.
(e) The license of the sexually oriented businesses shall be classified as follows, based upon the information in the application and subject to subsequent inspection for verification:
(1) Adult bookstore;
(2) Adult cabaret;
(3) Adult semi-nude modeling studio;
(4) Adult movie theater;
(5) Adult video facility;
(6) Adult video store; or
(7) Sexual device shop.
(Ord. of 05-07-2018(2))
